  "Question": "Bag A contains three chips labeled \\(1,\\) \\(3,\\) and \\(5.\\) Bag B contains three chips labeled \\(2,\\) \\(4,\\) and \\(6.\\) If one chip is drawn from each bag, how many different values are possible for the sum of the two numbers on the chips?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(5\\)",
    "C": "\\(6\\)",
    "D": "\\(7\\)",
    "E": "\\(9\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Fix the chip from Bag A and add each possible chip from Bag B. Drawing \\(1\\) from Bag A gives sums \\(3,5,7\\); drawing \\(3\\) gives \\(5,7,9\\); drawing \\(5\\) gives \\(7,9,11\\).\n\nThis includes every pairing because all three choices from Bag A have been paired with all three choices from Bag B. Counting each sum value only once leaves\n\\[\n3,5,7,9,11.\n\\]\nThere are \\(5\\) different values, choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
